WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/system/components/status/TeslaAuthCard.tsx — a PURE PRESENTATIONAL card (props:
  authenticated?: bool, expiresAt?: ISO string, now: number). Always rendered (operator-grade visibility); the
  styling intensifies healthy → amber (≤7d) → red (expired/disconnected). Uses @/components/ui {GlassPanel, Badge}.

    severityFor(authenticated, expiresAt, now):
      authenticated === false               → 'disconnected'
      !expiresAt                            → 'unknown'
      !Number.isFinite(Date.parse(exp))     → 'unknown'
      days = Math.floor((exp - now)/86_400_000); days < 0 → 'expired'; days <= 7 → 'warn'; else 'ok'
    TONE[sev]   = bar/icon tint + label {Connected | Expires soon | Token expired | Not connected | Unknown}
                  + badge {success | warning | danger | danger | neutral} + Icon {ShieldCheck|ShieldAlert|ShieldX}
    detail      = disconnected → "No Tesla account is currently connected."
                  !expiresAt   → "Token expiry unknown — re-authenticate to refresh."
                  unparseable  → "Token expiry unparseable."
                  ms<0 → ago=floor(-ms/86_400_000); ago===0 ? "Expired today — …Fleet API calls."
                                                              : "Expired {ago}d ago — …Fleet API calls."
                  days=floor(ms/86_400_000); 0 → "Token expires later today."; 1 → "Token expires in 1 day.";
                                             else "Token expires in {days} days."
    CTA         = (sev==='expired' || sev==='disconnected') ? "Re-authenticate" : "Manage"  →  <Link to="/tesla-account">
  Golden values (from web/src/.../__tests__/TeslaAuthCard.test.tsx, NOW=2025-01-15T12:00:00Z):
    (true,+30d)→"Connected"/"Token expires in 30 days."/"Manage"→/tesla-account · (true,+5d)→"Expires soon"/
    "Token expires in 5 days." · (true,-2d)→"Token expired"/"Re-authenticate" · (false,∅)→"Not connected"/
    "No Tesla account is currently connected."/"Re-authenticate" · (true,∅)→"Unknown".
  i18n  : the web source is "anonymous" (hardcoded English literals, no t() calls). Per the native
          no-English-literals rule every literal is promoted to a P1/S10 key (table "TeslaAuthCard").

